<h1>Conveyor Components: Parts of a Conveyor System</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">Conveyor components are the parts that make up a conveyor system: the frame, the conveying surface (belt, rollers, or chain), the drive, the pulleys and take-up that hold tension, the bearings, the product handling accessories such as guide rails, the sensors and controls, and the guarding. This page maps each category, what drives its specification, and where to go for detail. For how frame, drive, and pulley choices are sized together during a new design, see <a href="/resources/conveyor-design-guide/components/">how to specify frames, drives, and pulleys in conveyor design</a>.</p>
